/div> </div> </div>They were Kickstarter Rewards.<br /> <br /> Been getting this error sometimes, it double posts.<br /> <br /> Anyways, insert joke about Uratha cookbook 'To Serve Man.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T11:07:56-07:00","id":1151979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks#post1151894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or were these KS rewards?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were Kickstarter Rewards.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T11:22:34-07:00","id":1151982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1151971#post1151971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to Dine: The Ultimate Ashwood Abbey Recipe Book<br /> <br /> A Thousand and One Arabian Elixers<br /> <br /> Operation TWILIGHT Field Survival Guide</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think the AA would rather have a wine-pairing list of what to savor before/after a hunt. Reds when hunting vampires, etc. (And tequila post Mage hunting to wash away the Dissonance induced trauma).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T13:44:14-07:00","id":1152010,"title":"","content":"Considering I have been chopping one away at the recipes in the Apocalypse Cookbook recently, I can tell you exactly why we need more Cookbooks, particularly for Chronicles.<br /> <br /> 1) Cooking is fun! Having a book of recipes in general is a fun way to get on your feet and begin learning it if you haven't done it, and as you do it you start getting into it, you get the joy of experimenting and trying new things-I'm already coming up with ideas on how to do better than Damper Bread for the Bunyip, which brings me around to my next argument...<br /> <br /> 2) Much like music, prop pieces, and many other things, cooking a recipe tailored to a gaming session is a a great way to establish a mood for games, and having books that helped to build on the pre-existing in game packages of moods in the forms of y-splats or z-splats or individual cities or whatever make gives you a pre-made toolkit for inspiration in case you don't want to come up with a individual dishes for session, instead pairing them up based on what you have. I have a recipe I'm working on(Human Hearts and Poison Apples) that I know, once I get it right, I cannot conceive of trying to pitch Changeling The Lost without serving it alongside it, and considering the duel themes of Paris, I think my projects after that will be figuring out dishes for each of the Rosiere Courts.<br /> <br /> 3) It's a great human layer to add to any supernatural society you want. The Recipes in the Apocalypse Cookbook were more nuanced and interesting approaches to each of the tribes that made them feel more real, far less cartoonish, and more human-and the Chronicles of Darkness is even more deeply rooted in the sense of the human, even when it's in rejection of it. By taking a franchise that is all about that place in between and the transition from one to other and giving it a very human place to show a face in, it allows for further richness and contextualization of those characters.<br /> <br /> Take, for instance, the jab at Beasts. Sure, the big thing for them is that they eat the shock that they generate by acting against humanity...but they still need to eat regular food too. But on top of that, the way they live their lives as Beasts surely colors their culinary tastes and relates their Legends and nightmares with their Lives and connections. Imagine how two different Giants approach a main course, communicating intense, overpowering flavours that never the less are enjoyable to have wash over you, to communicate hopelessness, and the ways that changes from places to place, person to person. How do varying Nemesis play around with saltiness, bitterness, sourness, and spicyness when trying to slyly communicate things to their prey, and what do their choices say when the only person they're serving is themselves? Questions like these humanize one of the most contentious splats in fandom and at the same time allow their themes to be reinforced in things we get, that we're intrinsically familiar with, all while giving an angle for something different for your night.<br /> <br /> 4) The Chronicles world is <i>rife</i> with opportunity for cool recipe ideas, even as it's wider spread forms embrace a powerful homogeny. It has both strange niches and strong ideals that weave in and out of a wide variety of cultural contexts and momentary moods and philosophical viewpoints that can be powerfully expressed in food. Consider how a <i>certain someone's</i> problems with reconciling how the Diamond and Free Council approach culture could possibly be answer by showing how the Silver Ladder and the Free Council approach an Indian recipe, for example. There's room and ability and divergence to both re-tell and re-examine the stories we're familiar with <i>and</i> make really cool food.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, more cookbooks, please, and particularly let's get started on Chronicles based dishes. In fact, I'll be openly disappointed if Changeling the Lost's kickstarter does <i>not</i> have a stretch goal for a cookbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T13:53:40-07:00","id":1152013,"title":"","content":"I'd rather they spend their rather limited time on books that are more useful. Each gameline can only get one book for per two to four years, I'd rather something I can use rather than something which sounds like a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:02:26-07:00","id":1152018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1152013#post1152013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather they spend their rather limited time on books that are more useful. Each gameline can only get one book for per two to four years, I'd rather something I can use rather than something which sounds like a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but a) it's only sounds like a joke, but the Apocalypse Cookbook turned out to be an impressive bit of fluff with a lot of character and insight in there(and if you're the sort of person who thinks fluff isn't worth it, cool, can't help you, think you're wrong), b) Cookbooks are often only worked on by one or two people in terms of writing(Stew, I think, pretty explicitly made Apocalypse Cookbook all by himself, and the Ascension Cookbook doesn't sound like it has any more people on it, from what little has been said reveals), and while editting, layout, and art is more people, that's not exactly a limit, c) THey are deliberately placed as low priority, because it takes time to find and make recipes that work and the people working on them are often working on All Manner Of Other Shit, but also d) they aren't that big of a book anyways, so food work asides, it's not much to actually write up, and e) most of the writing staff enjoys cooking anyways, so experimenting with food for dinner becoming part of the job is not particularly a time-waster.<br /> <br /> I get the sentiment about it distracting from 'important' books, but, uh, I don't think it's anywhere near the problem you think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:24:43-07:00","id":1152025,"title":"","content":"IId like to see a requiem cocktail book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:26:36-07:00","id":1152027,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> i totally agree with you, forgive me the pun but the cookbooks add more flavor to the setting, and potentially to a session!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T16:52:53-07:00","id":1152058,"title":"","content":"In an effort to add something to the awesomeness that was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> on this:<br /> <br /> Cookbooks are like the VtR Clanbooks or Secret of the Covenants. They make the game more full and lived in. They're not about more little rules (which are still good things to have), they're not about deep diving into specific topics, they're about showing the &quot;reality&quot; of the game universe.<br /> <br /> I agree that there's more challenge in the CofD games because you can't frame things as easily as the WoD games can with a lot of their splats. But just like the games themselves, there's more freedom there too. Without having to go, &quot;The Black Furies are Greek based culturally, so we need to reflect that,&quot; thinking about what to do gets more interesting because you have to look elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Imagine the really interesting detail you'd get out of The Pack, where we learn of a favorite dish for each of the sample packs? What does the Spirit Machine serve at late night coding sessions? What's Engine-22's chili like? Does die Gaedestra\u00dfebande have a dish that one of the Wolfblooded makes just for those on long watches? What's the comfort food that La Clinica's kitchen puts out to remind people of good times?<br /> <br /> Those might seem like little details... but little details can mean a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T00:00:25-07:00","id":1152127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1152018#post1152018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, but a) it's only sounds like a joke, but the Apocalypse Cookbook turned out to be an impressive bit of fluff with a lot of character and insight in there(and if you're the sort of person who thinks fluff isn't worth it, cool, can't help you, think you're wrong), b) Cookbooks are often only worked on by one or two people in terms of writing(Stew, I think, pretty explicitly made Apocalypse Cookbook all by himself, and the Ascension Cookbook doesn't sound like it has any more people on it, from what little has been said reveals), and while editting, layout, and art is more people, that's not exactly a limit, c) THey are deliberately placed as low priority, because it takes time to find and make recipes that work and the people working on them are often working on All Manner Of Other Shit, but also d) they aren't that big of a book anyways, so food work asides, it's not much to actually write up, and e) most of the writing staff enjoys cooking anyways, so experimenting with food for dinner becoming part of the job is not particularly a time-waster.<br /> <br /> I get the sentiment about it distracting from 'important' books, but, uh, I don't think it's anywhere near the problem you think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>a) I'm fine with fluff, just not fluff about something so ridiculously specific and mundane. Most of the time, supernaturals are going to be eating the same food as everyone else in their culture. Even if you ignore the tiny tiny tiny tiny scope of &quot;Cookbook for a serious gothic horror game&quot;, you have the issue of culture not being as homogenous in CofD as it is in WoD so each dish will probably be basically limited to a very specific part of the world and be even more useless.<br /> <br /> b) That's still people that could be making something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T10:47:22-07:00","id":1152232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1151962#post1151962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , so it's literal cook book... &lt;Rolling Eyes&gt; Why would <b><i>any </i></b>gameline of CoD need one? MAYBE <b>Beast: The Primodrial </b>'<i>How to best cook your victims Fears'</i>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> This, so much this.<br /> <br /> I mean its not 17 pages of names as filler bad (Xanather's Guide to Everything I'm looking at you), its still WTF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T11:04:52-07:00","id":1152238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1152232#post1152232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean its not 17 pages of names as filler bad (Xanather's Guide to Everything I'm looking at you), its still WTF.</div> </div> </div> </div>...the book that's not even out yet and is going to have a higher page count then 17? Right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T12:09:39-07:00","id":1153549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151894-cookbooks?p=1152127#post1152127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> a) I'm fine with fluff, just not fluff about something so ridiculously specific and mundane. Most of the time, supernaturals are going to be eating the same food as everyone else in their culture. Even if you ignore the tiny tiny tiny tiny scope of &quot;Cookbook for a serious gothic horror game&quot;, you have the issue of culture not being as homogenous in CofD as it is in WoD so each dish will probably be basically limited to a very specific part of the world and be even more useless.<br /> <br /> b) That's still people that could be making something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Phallic's comment is useless, let's break this down.<br /> <br /> A1*) I sort of get the argument against specific, but mundane? Mundane is significant part of most of these games. I mean, just look at Touchstones-that entire mechanic exists to ensure that your character has these stupid, quiet moments. Virtue and Vices tend to get acted out in the small scale, and at least one of each splat's anchors tend to be a call to pull back and grab something at Denny's before you lose yourself in the red, red meat. Changeling is all about sacrificing the miraculous for the mundane, that you have traded the beautiful and terrible that you will always shudder before for the sincerity and connection of a gas station burrito handed to you by a co-worker and idle conversation and dumb jokes with the neighborhood punk kids who play their glam-gangster rap too loud. Prometheans find themselves in the awkward office parties and stupid Netflix and Chill moments. Sin-Eaters defy death because that fucking report is going to end up on the bosses desk. Demons fall because there's just something in the way he moves and smiles, and you could buy these greasy fries all day just to watch his hips, or because god <i>damn</i> there's just this smell here in the alley between the theater and the dive bar that gets you. I could go on, but my point is that ChroD's humanism <i>is</i> a recognition of the value and power in the mundane, and many other facets of it's take on the subject do connect to it. Hell, if i thought about it more, I could probably even support that mechanically.<br /> <br /> A2) Sure, people will eat what's in their culture, but personality and tastes seep into any dish. When I eat tamago kake gohan, I tend to double down on the eggs and add cheddar and bacon, where as when my roommate eats it he tends to add more spicy additions. Subcultures within societies take their cultural cornerstones and put their spins on it, and imagining the way that supernatural subcultures would do that and seeing how that actually translates on paper makes for a really enjoyable perspective.<br /> <br /> A3a) With Chronicles featuring more cities with each book than they did before with their own unique problems and personal cultures, I don't think the homogenity is the same problem it used to be on that front. A dish for each of the Rosiere Courts in Paris would be different from a dish for each of the Seasonal Courts in Miami, which would be different from the Seasonal Courts in Baltimore, and all of those would be different from the Market Courts in New Orleans, as an example. And on Seasonal being in their twice...<br /> <br /> A3b) While that homogenity can be a problem, there are still strong avenues to explore in the form of Chronicles strong thematic emphasis. As mentioned in my first big rant, There's a difference in the way two Giants in different parts of the world would express their ties to hopelessness in a satisfyingly freeing way through food. Similarly, while a Libertine and a Thearch have their own reasons to honor Indian culture, the way they, as magicians, perceive the world will drastically affect the way they decide to present that culture through food. All we've done is trade location for ideas(except not really, see the above), and made a scenario in which ideas are probably better expressed through multiple variations. None of that is a problem.<br /> <br /> B) People have to eat, and a lot of people on this staff will stop and take the hour or two to actually cook the meal, and maybe even experiment with it. The meat of work on a Cookbook is not time you are losing to other books, it is time gained by taking advantage of a timeframe you were already losing out to. Simply put, the &quot;time eating&quot; is not a problem.<br /> <br /> Look, it is a curiosity, definitely a niche-but it's a highly enjoyable and usable niche for a lot of adults, and that keeps it from being a joke like some people seem to think here. It may not be your cup of tea, but the fact that there was enough interest in it to happen <i>twice</i> already indicates that a lot of people are actually down for it, and apparently financial support is there, no one at OPP seems bothered by how it will affect games. Everything I've told you about production and how much of not a problem it is is cited from Stew on the Apocalypse one, and the few comments I've heard about Ascension's indicates that the opinion is continuing to be held. And we have the space to do it in ChroD, and even from a refreshingly different approach.<br /> <br /> And, again, both times we've gotten the product, it has been way down the list of stretch goals. This isn't something idly done.<br /> <br /> So, I get you, I know where you're coming from? But, uh. Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> *Neither the steak sauce nor the animation studio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T14:45:32-07:00","id":1154517,"title":"","content":"And proving my point, the M20 Cookbook varies as much on theme as it does on region.<br /> <br /> Also holy shit this is a much bigger book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T16:18:58-07:00","id":1154539,"title":"","content":"any idea when it will be available to non backers in dead tree format?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:28:15-07:00","id":1154557,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say? The W20 Cookbook didn't take that long to get to non-backers, but it's also a shorter book.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine it's going to be that long. Usually the open period for errata is around a month, and assuming a cookbook doesn't need much errata and re-layout and all that, I'd be surprised if it wasn't ready by the end of the year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}